1
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:37,910
Freedom

2
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,500
Arnheid.

3
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:42,560
Which means this is Ketil's farm.

4
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:46,150
I don't believe it.

5
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:50,360
The two of you were just
a few days' walk away.

6
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,720
You look a little haggard...

7
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:59,720
But you're even more beautiful than before.

8
00:02:06,110 --> 00:02:10,740
What? Is he Arnheid's husband?

9
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,310
Is Hjalti doing well?

10
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:22,750
He must be so big by now.

11
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:33,750
Gardar...

12
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:37,780
Hjalti is...

13
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:47,140
Come.

14
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,960
Let's return to our home together.
All three of us.

15
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,360
Our home?

16
00:02:57,490 --> 00:02:59,870
Don't take his hand, Arnheid.

17
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:09,110
If you do, I'll kill him.

18
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:26,520
Gardar!

19
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,190
Fox!

20
00:03:28,190 --> 00:03:30,140
Take Arnheid and get out of here.

21
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:31,110
Yes, boss.

22
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:41,260
There's something wrong with him, boss.

23
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:44,400
Did he forget he's being chased?

24
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:49,290
Is it true that he killed Lizard?

25
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:55,270
Yes. Split his head wide open.

26
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:58,400
I see.

27
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,220
He's here to kidnap Arnheid.

28
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:06,080
Protect her with your life.

29
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:06,840
Yes, boss.

30
00:04:09,230 --> 00:04:11,110
Are you Ketil?

31
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:15,760
What if I am?

32
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:19,410
I'll kill you!

33
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:23,240
Stop, Gardar! This is reckless!

34
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,880
Gardar!

35
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:35,320
Don't, Einar.

36
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:37,840
We don't even know what's going on.
What are you going to do?

37
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:40,510
Are you going to attack Snake?

38
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:42,760
I know exactly what's going on here!

39
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:46,640
Arnheid's husband is here to rescue her.

40
00:04:47,050 --> 00:04:50,400
Don't you want her to be free?

41
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:53,300
I do, but look at what you're dealing with.

42
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,780
You'd have to kill three men to get away.

43
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:59,260
I know I'm not strong enough, but...

44
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:02,470
Einar, that's not what I'm trying to say.

45
00:05:03,350 --> 00:05:05,320
Can you kill a man?

46
00:05:05,770 --> 00:05:08,160
Whether it's a guest or anyone else,

47
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,690
could you use this axe to kill a man?

48
00:05:16,610 --> 00:05:21,600
Then... what am I supposed to do?

49
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:26,140
Smart choice, Thorfinn.

50
00:05:27,170 --> 00:05:29,390
You guys watch quietly from over there.

51
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:32,820
I'll capture him alive.

52
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:36,770
I still need to question him
and confirm his identity.

53
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:48,790
Be careful, boss. He's strong.

54
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:54,150
Who do you think you're talking to, dumbass?

55
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:57,520
Whoa.

56
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:06,010
You can't take him alive, boss. Kill him.

57
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:10,600
Shut up. That was just a warm-up.

58
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:14,480
Were you guys able to land
a single blow on him?

59
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:18,230
What? Well, embarrassingly...

60
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,810
He's injured.

61
00:06:21,810 --> 00:06:25,460
How'd the three of you lose
to an injured man?

62
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,000
So that's where it was after all.

63
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,870
Badger, tie him up.

64
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:54,290
Gardar! Gardar!

65
00:06:51,830 --> 00:06:55,020
Wow, you beat him in an instant.

66
00:06:56,670 --> 00:06:58,800
Gardar!

67
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,190
Arnheid!

68
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:09,030
Arnheid!

69
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,120
Arnheid!

70
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:19,090
Arnheid!

71
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:19,430
Come on, walk.

72
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:23,880
Don't let your guard down.

73
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:27,270
Always keep five guys watching him.

74
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:27,270
Arnheid!

75
00:07:27,270 --> 00:07:32,440
And tell Kjallakr's uncle that
we've apprehended the suspect.

76
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,440
Arnheid!

77
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,650
Got it.

78
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,600
Now then...

79
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:44,180
You look like you've got something to say.

80
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:47,160
But a slave's opinion doesn't matter.

81
00:07:51,230 --> 00:07:53,060
Can't you let him off the hook?

82
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:55,920
This is too much to bear.

83
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:58,570
He killed one of my men.

84
00:07:58,570 --> 00:08:00,790
He's suspected of killing others, too.

85
00:08:02,510 --> 00:08:05,160
Not only that,
but he wants to kill the master,

86
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:08,420
and he intends to kidnap
the master's darling Arnheid.

87
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:13,460
We can't let someone like that off the hook.

88
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:26,200
Forget about him, Arnheid.

89
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,950
That's not your husband.

90
00:08:29,430 --> 00:08:31,840
He's just a runaway slave
who's lost his mind.

91
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:42,760
Stay out of this matter.
Look after Gramps for me.

92
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:26,740
Einar, wait.

93
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:27,730
Einar.

94
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:34,560
Please have a seat.

95
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:39,700
It's almost time for dinner.

96
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,460
At night, under cover of darkness,

97
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:51,490
we might be able to sneak into
the fort and rescue Gardar.

98
00:09:52,590 --> 00:09:56,880
If we don't do something,
your husband will be executed.

99
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:02,580
Thank you, but it's all right.

100
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,760
Sometimes, things can't be changed.

101
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:11,970
And it's better not to do
anything in those situations.

102
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:17,860
It's better to sit still and
wait for the storm to pass.

103
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:23,510
I don't want you to get
caught in the storm, Einar.

104
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:32,120
Don't you love Gardar?

105
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:34,630
I do.

106
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:43,190
Our parents arranged our marriage,
but he was kind to me and our son.

107
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:46,870
Then we should go.

108
00:10:46,870 --> 00:10:50,900
Even if we end up having to fight Snake
and his men, it's better than doing nothing.

109
00:10:51,650 --> 00:10:53,650
Isn't that right, Thorfinn?

110
00:10:57,180 --> 00:11:00,200
Please, Thorfinn. Lend me your strength.

111
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:02,540
I'll draw the guards to me, so you...

112
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:07,270
I lost my son because of pots.

113
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:18,710
Could I tell you a little about myself?

114
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:31,270
About the past.

115
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:04,020
Our family lived in a village in Sweden.

116
00:12:05,070 --> 00:12:09,730
Neither wealthy nor poor,
we lived a quiet life.

117
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,960
When our son was one year old,

118
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:23,990
deep in a distant forest,
a marsh containing iron was found.

119
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:32,080
Fighting broke out between several groups
competing for ownership of the marsh.

120
00:12:33,590 --> 00:12:37,610
Gardar's friend was among
those involved in the conflict,

121
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,850
and he asked for his help.

122
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:49,630
Gardar told the rest of the village about it,
and the men gathered to discuss it.

123
00:12:50,590 --> 00:12:53,670
Should we join the fighting or not?

124
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:57,130
If we won, we'd acquire iron.

125
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:06,740
So the men decided to join the fight.

126
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:18,660
The women were shocked when we heard this.

127
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:25,560
After all, our village had all the
pots and sickle blades we needed.

128
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:34,950
But women can't overturn
a decision made by men.

129
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:40,680
Please reconsider, Gardar.

130
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:44,340
It's not as though we're currently
suffering from a lack of iron.

131
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:51,730
Why are you risking your life
for something we don't need?

132
00:13:52,590 --> 00:13:53,880
Arnheid.

133
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:58,130
We do need it.

134
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:03,660
Yngve of the West is an ambitious man.

135
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:09,910
If his clan acquires the iron, it'll upset
the balance of power in the area.

136
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:16,280
And our village will become wealthy.

137
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:18,980
So will the two of you.

138
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:35,110
Hjalti, your father is going to
fight to protect you.

139
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:39,530
I couldn't understand it.

140
00:14:39,530 --> 00:14:41,060
Ow, that hurts.

141
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:47,600
He could've protected us
better by staying with us.

142
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:58,450
All the young men went off to battle,

143
00:14:58,890 --> 00:15:01,960
while the women and children were
left behind to defend our homes.

144
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:04,220
Several weeks passed.

145
00:15:06,190 --> 00:15:07,350
And then...

146
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,730
Look.

147
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:21,120
When we saw the ships,
we thought the men had returned.

148
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,600
But instead...

149
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:41,810
They attacked while the men were gone.

150
00:15:43,650 --> 00:15:47,190
Our homes were burned.
The elderly were killed.

151
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:52,870
The women were put on ships and taken away.

152
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:59,010
And I... lost Hjalti...

153
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:16,370
Hjalti! No! Hjalti!

154
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:35,940
When I met Gardar today, I was afraid of him.

155
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:42,000
I'm sure all the suffering
he's experienced has changed him.

156
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:47,410
He is the storm itself now.

157
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:59,010
This time, I must protect my child,
from the men's storm.

158
00:17:02,050 --> 00:17:03,830
Your child?

159
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:09,330
I just learned the other day

160
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:15,640
that I'm pregnant with Master Ketil's child.

161
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:24,610
I'm sure he'll welcome this child.

162
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,600
After all, he's been wanting one.

163
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:37,160
On this farm, I could peacefully
raise a healthy child.

164
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,380
So Einar,

165
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:48,790
stay here until the storm passes.

166
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,600
Stay here.

167
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:58,660
I thought you were waiting
for the storm to pass, Arnheid.

168
00:19:01,090 --> 00:19:04,200
You were listening, sir?

169
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:11,260
You seem to think I've gone
completely senile,

170
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:15,300
but I haven't lost my senses yet.
Don't underestimate me.

171
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:24,320
I thought I could at least tend his wounds.

172
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:35,200
I know I shouldn't see him again,

173
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:40,050
so why?

174
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:52,480
I once patiently waited
for a storm to pass, too.

175
00:19:55,660 --> 00:20:02,470
No, I trembled as I hid.

176
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:19,700
It was more than 20 years ago.

177
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:30,610
My son Ketil and a beautiful girl from
our village were in love back then.

178
00:20:33,790 --> 00:20:39,300
But one day, a man from
a nearby village named Ebbe

179
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:43,060
who'd been growing his power
fell in love with her,

180
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:46,690
and I was forced to make a painful decision.

181
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:53,680
Ketil was prepared to fight to protect her.

182
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:59,430
But at the time, we were still weak.

183
00:20:59,430 --> 00:21:02,760
Many were afraid of Ebbe.

184
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:06,610
They thought we'd be
wiped out if we defied him.

185
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:14,870
So we made the decision to submit.

186
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:21,830
Norse men would be disgusted to hear that.

187
00:21:22,310 --> 00:21:27,750
I offered up a young woman to protect myself.

188
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:37,160
And yet, on the day of her wedding...

189
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:58,360
It was the work of a man who
envied and resented Ebbe's wealth.

190
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:06,210
By the time I heard
the news and rushed there,

191
00:22:06,750 --> 00:22:11,130
everything had already burned to ashes.

192
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:27,890
Why? Why does this always happen?

193
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:37,210
The only thing I can say is...

194
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:49,040
Even if you can wait out the storm,
it leaves scars behind.

195
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:08,020
I'm sorry I can't help you.

196
00:23:22,690 --> 00:23:25,240
I'll be back soon.

197
00:25:36,850 --> 00:25:39,730
Storm

198
00:25:37,730 --> 00:25:38,800
"Storm."
